       ⚠ THAT IS A DIFFERENT SITE FROM MS-5's, which is getText() on a null
       this at GroupItem.mm:1322. Two distinct crashes, not one.
       It is not installed because a fixture must not be able to delete the
       rest of the suite (rule H5) and this one would take the sentinel with
       it. The control is RECORDED rather than run: the `?` rows above mean
       something because this run shows the no-`?` spelling refusing to win.
       It carries its own row, docs/fixIts.md F-104.

    2. THE EMPTY DRIVE IS NOT EXPRESSIBLE, so optT("") is not a third row.
       Kant has no empty strings (bear-trap #28, reclassified as doctrine): a
       literal with no characters carries no data and a field with no data
       returns its own TAG. Measured -- optT("") reads
           MARKARM drive base=0x1048a9626 len=9 text=[quoteBody]
       so it drives the nine-character string `quoteBody`, `one` fails on `q`,
       optT does not fire, and the run exits 0 having tested nothing. A row
       here would be a row about the word quoteBody.

    3. repT's NEW-ROAD CELL cannot live in this file. parser() is a one-way
       door and MS-5 crashes before it, so the generated repT body and its
       new-road cursor reading are taken in tester.
***************************************************************************/
